meta {
  name: Nodes - List (Global Catalog)
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/nodes
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~category: slack
  ~search: post_message
}

docs {
  The global built-in catalog only — no workspace needed, no custom
  nodes merged in (those are inherently workspace-scoped). Use this to
  browse "what nodes exist" before a workspace is picked; once one is,
  `Nodes - List (Workspace)` is the one to call instead, since it also
  merges in that workspace's custom nodes.

  Each entry now also carries `icon`/`color` (inherited from the node's
  category) and `requires_connector` (whether the node needs a
  workspace `ConnectorCredential` to run).

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { nodes } }`.
}
